    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1255" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδήρι-τος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>without strife</i> or
				<i>battle</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				17.42
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>uncontested, undisputed</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				1.2.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>A.</u>
				846
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδηρί-τως</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				3.93.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				4.14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Caes.</u>
				3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>not to be striven against, unconquerable</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνάγκης σθένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					105
				</span></i>
			.</div>
